<title>JAMAICA: Jamaica to join Caracas-based development bank.</title>
<headline>Jamaica to join Caracas-based development bank.</headline>
<dateline>KINGSTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jamaica will sign a membership agreement Friday with the Corporacion Andino de Fomento (CAF), becoming the second Caribbean nation to join the Caracas-based development bank, the government announced in a press release.</p>
<p>Jamaica applied for membership in July 1994 as a shareholder, in order to benefit from CAF's facilities for strengthening foreign trade and assisting companies in accessing foreign markets.</p>
<p>Trinidad is already a member of CAF, as are Brazil, Chile, Paraguay, Mexico and the five member-states of the Andean Pact: Colombia, Venezuela, Peru, Ecuador, and Bolivia.</p>
</text>
